title: "NeusktchmechArc: A Personal Provenance Transmuting Feeling into Form"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Bhatara"
    given-names: "Mohit"
abstract: >
  The repository documents the NeusktchmechArc artistic framework, a distinct
  part of an independently maintained personal creative, biographical, and
  scholarly archive. The artistic framework is a fictional and internally
  constructed reference space through which lived impressions are described
  as gradually taking visual form. Its principal self-authored conceptual
  references include Interior Atlas, First Emanation, Tranquil Rift, and
  Integration Phase. These references are descriptive and contextual rather
  than stages of a transferable method. The artistic framework is presented
  as a non-commercial creative work solely for contextual understanding and
  reflection, not for instruction, application, adoption, diagnosis, guidance,
  or professional use.
